course: dictionary
lesson: 12171
title: Hidden in plain sight: concealed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Concealed means hidden, kept out of sight. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues. «The door was concealed behind the bookcase.» The door is hard to see because a bookcase is in front of it, so concealed must mean hidden.
explain: Concealed can also be the past form of the verb conceal. «The pirates concealed their gold in a cave.» The pirates hid the gold, and they kept it secret. To check, swap in the word hid: «The pirates hid their gold in a cave.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You will see concealed on safety signs too. «Concealed entrance» warns that a way in is hard to see, so drivers need to take care. In nature, animals use camouflage to stay concealed from predators, and in stories, secret doors and treasure are often concealed.
fact: Concealed means hidden, kept out of sight.
fact: Concealed can be an adjective, as in «a concealed door», or the past form of the verb conceal, as in «She concealed the key».
fact: «Well concealed» means hidden very carefully, so it is very hard to see.
fact: «Concealed from view» means you cannot see it at all.
fact: A «concealed entrance» or «concealed driveway» on a sign warns drivers that cars may come out from somewhere hard to see.
exercise: «The door was concealed behind the bookcase.» What does concealed mean here? | Open and easy to find | *Hidden, out of sight | Painted bright red | Made of glass
exercise: A road sign says «Concealed driveway». What does the sign warn drivers about? | Cars must drive very fast | *Cars may come out from somewhere hard to see | There is a shop with a big sale | The road is closed for a party
exercise: «The pirates concealed their gold in a cave.» What did the pirates do with the gold? | *Hid it and kept it secret | Spent it all on sweets | Showed it to everyone in the village | Gave it to the king
test: «The rabbit was well concealed in the long grass.» Which word is closest in meaning to concealed? | Loud | *Hidden | Empty | Visible
test: Which phrase means a way in that is hard to see? | Bright sign | Open gate | Wide road | *Concealed entrance
exam: «Mia concealed the letter under her pillow.» What does concealed mean? | Read aloud to everyone | *Hidden, kept out of sight | Thrown out of the window | Torn into small pieces
